From 6fe54cccc4d5d169e7f049961b2c807b82d4e518 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:09:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(http): honor configured and server retry delays

Keep HTTP error classification and retry limits intact while carrying a per-request retry delay. Respect Retry-After on 429 and 503 using the existing HTTP date parser and a 600-second cap. Preserve dedicated status controls and skip sleeping requests when the segment scheduler searches for a faster pooled connection.

Inspiration: aria2-next retry scheduling (https://github.com/AnInsomniacy/aria2-next/blob/1b8fb72fcf63dc9e78807f20039708184bce0ad2/src/http/HttpTask.cc). Implemented against aria2 APIs.
